notes.body:
Nighty build is good enough.

I have sent multiple emails to tcpdump-workers@lists.tcpdump.org without any response. I don't know if there is other way to ask for it.

@guyharris, are you helping on this?

![mbim-etl](/uploads/e4c5b3fa9cfcb32b57734303f995972a/mbim-etl.png)

@graham.bloice , here is the attachment for your and everyone else's reference how it works with change change.

With this function, you can see how convenient it would be in the future for the developers who works on MBIM.

@crondaemon, hopefully you can successfully test this PR. As I mentioned before, I was preparing another PR that can dissect event message from etl in addition to MBIM message. Now https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/697 was pushed for your reference, you can also test it to see how it works to show the event message in addition to MBIM message. Again, in the future, based on this solution, IP packets from etl will be added.

Also attach a screenshot for your reference without compiling the PR
![mbim-message-etl](/uploads/cf52ad4fc3ca1bfef30b69212ea0dafc/mbim-message-etl.PNG)

all those lines can be resumed to
`uuid_idx = mbim_dissect_service_id_uuid(frag_tvb, pinfo, mbim_tree, hf_mbim_device_service_id, &offset, &uuid_ext_info, pinfo->rec->rec_header.packet_header.pkt_encap != WTAP_ENCAP_ETL);
`

